<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gregory the Patrician</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 647</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Gregory, Exarch of Africa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gregory the Patrician was the Byzantine exarch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> and a relative of the Heraclian dynasty. Opposing the Monothelete religious policy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constans-ii">Constans II</a>, he proclaimed himself emperor in 646. He was killed in 647 when an Arab army defeated him at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufetula">Sufetula</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sbeitla">Sbeitla</a>) in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a>, the first major Arab invasion of the province.</p></div>
